---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from 'astro:i18n';
const tutorialUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/tutorial/');
const directoryUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/plugins/directory/');
const noatmarkUrl = 'https://github.com/ylwl1997/noatmark-dsh-plugin';
const noatmarkNpmUrl = 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/noatmark-dsh-plugin';
const topicUrl = 'https://github.com/topics/dsh-plugin';
---
<Base
  title="DeepSeek Harness Plugins — Everything-is-a-Plugin Development | dshbase"
  description="Build DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugins: what a plugin is, your first plugin with cordis.yml, registering tools with defineTool, and publishing to the dsh-plugin ecosystem."
  currentPath="/plugins/"
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plugins</p>
    <h1>Everything is a <span class="accent">plugin.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">DeepSeek Harness's defining idea: every capability is a plugin. Learn what a plugin is, write your first one, and register tools. Based on the official developer guide.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap dir-banner">
    <a class="dir-banner-inner" href={directoryUrl}>
      <div>
        <span class="cat">Plugin directory</span>
        <h3>Browse 123 community plugins — with test results &amp; install commands</h3>
        <p>Every plugin's npm status, verified test result, and exact <code>dsh plugin add</code> command, all in one place.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="btn btn-primary">Open the directory &rarr;</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="info wrap">
    <h2>What is a <span class="accent">plugin?</span></h2>
    <p>A Harness plugin is a TypeScript module that exports an <code>apply</code> function. The framework calls <code>apply</code> when it loads, passing a <code>ctx</code> through which you register capabilities:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>import type &#123; Context &#125; from '@deepseek-ai/cordis'

export const name = 'my-plugin'

export function apply(ctx: Context) &#123;
  // Register capabilities here.
&#125;</code></pre>
    <p>Anything you register via <code>ctx</code> is cleaned up automatically when the plugin unloads.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:24px">Your first plugin</h2>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>mkdir -p scratch-plugin/src</code></pre>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>// scratch-plugin/src/my-plugin.ts
import type &#123; Context &#125; from '@deepseek-ai/cordis'
export const name = 'hello-plugin'
export function apply(ctx: Context) &#123;
  console.log('[hello-plugin] plugin loaded!')
&#125;</code></pre>
    <p>Create <code>scratch-plugin/cordis.yml</code> pointing at the absolute path, then start the Web UI with the patch:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>- insert:
    - id: hello
      name: '/absolute/path/to/deepseek-harness/scratch-plugin/src/my-plugin.ts'</code></pre>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>pnpm dsh web --patch ./scratch-plugin/cordis.yml</code></pre>

    <h2 style="margin-top:24px">Install &amp; use a community plugin</h2>
    <p>No code needed — plugins are npm packages. Add one to a profile (requires pnpm):</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-claude-marketplace</code></pre>
    <p>DSH installs the package, records it in the profile's <code>package.json</code> (dependency + <code>dsh.profile.bundles</code>), and loads it on the next <code>dsh web</code> launch. Confirm with <code>dsh plugin --profile web list</code>, remove with <code>dsh plugin --profile web remove &lt;package&gt;</code>. Real npm plugins to try: <code>noatmark-dsh-plugin</code> (text hygiene tools), <code>dsh-claude-marketplace</code> (load your <code>.claude</code> skills &amp; commands), <code>dsh-plugin-session-import</code> (import Claude Code / Codex history), <code>dsh-fail-logger</code>, <code>dsh-latex-tools</code>, <code>dsh-cloudflare-browser-run</code>. Search the ecosystem with <code>npm search dsh-plugin</code>.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:24px">Register a tool</h2>
    <p>Use <code>defineTool</code> to add a tool your agent can call:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>import &#123; defineTool &#125; from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools'

ctx.tools.register(defineTool(&#123;
  name: 'greet',
  description: 'Greet someone by name.',
  parameters: &#123; name: &#123; type: 'string', required: true, description: 'The name' &#125; &#125;,
  output: &#123; schema: &#123; type: 'string' &#125;, render: (_a, v) => [&#123; type: 'text', text: v &#125;] &#125;,
  async execute(args) &#123; return `Hello, $&#123;args.name&#125;!` &#125;,
&#125;))</code></pre>

    <h2 style="margin-top:24px">Community plugins &amp; publishing</h2>
    <p>Tag your repo with <a href={topicUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>dsh-plugin</code></a> to join the ecosystem, and see the <a href={directoryUrl}>plugin directory</a> (120+ curated).</p>
    <div class="grid3">
      <a class="card card-link" href={noatmarkNpmUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <span class="cat">Text hygiene · on npm</span>
        <h3>noatmark-dsh-plugin</h3>
        <p>Sanitize untrusted text, scan invisible chars, clean LLM formatting, and escape CSV injection. Install with <code>dsh plugin add noatmark-dsh-plugin</code>. <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></p>
      </a>
      <a class="card card-link" href={directoryUrl}>
        <span class="cat">Ecosystem</span>
        <h3>Plugin directory</h3>
        <p>120+ plugins across 7 categories. <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:20px"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href={tutorialUrl}>Back to the tutorial &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .dir-banner { margin: -10px auto 0; padding: 0 22px 8px; }
  .dir-banner-inner {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    background: linear-gradient(120deg, #eef2ff, #f6f8fc);
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 20px 24px;
    text-decoration: none; color: inherit;
  }
  .dir-banner-inner h3 { margin: 6px 0; font-size: 19px; color: var(--ink); }
  .dir-banner-inner p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 14px; }
  .dir-banner-inner .cat { color: var(--primary); font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px; }
</style>
